  "prefLabel": "Mhp 103.05 Committees",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mhp 103.05 Committees.\n\n(a) The Board may create an advisory committee for each mental health discipline license. The board member of each mental health discipline shall serve as the chair of that advisory committee. The remaining members shall include at least 2 licensees, and no more than 4 licensees in the mental health discipline of that committee.\n\n(b) The committee shall have no independent regulatory or disciplinary authority.\n\n(c) This section shall not affect or change the scope of practice of any mental health practice license.\n\nSource. #9852, eff 1-25-11 (formerly Mhp 103.06) (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Mhp 100); ss by #14182, eff 2-20-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mhp100.html"
